<title>USA: U.S. base metals and scrap prices - April 2.</title>
<headline>U.S. base metals and scrap prices - April 2.</headline>
<text>
<p>U.S. premiums added to LME official cash settlement price, except for copper, which is added to the COMEX spot month. Premium includes price for delivery to consumer's works.</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Aluminum: Western grade		   6.00-6.25 cents/pound</p>
<p>Zinc: Special high grade SHG	    5.50-6.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>Lead					    2.00-3.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>Tin   (Grade A)			     5.80-7.25 cents/pound</p>
<p>	(low lead, 50 ppm)		  7.25-8.25 cents/pound</p>
<p>Nickel (melting grade)		    9.00-12.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>Copper (high grade cathode)	     2.75-3.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Aluminum alloy (A380 grade), Midwest</p>
<p>and East coast, delivered to consumer     77-78 cents/pound</p>
<p>--</p>
